{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Working, plunder, crooked</b> — [vav-ḥet] three joined. And so it is: the working that working yields — wealth, treasures — is for the sake of a tongue of falsehood, for he testified falsely." "<b>A breath driven away</b> — the working of the multitude will depart, or the working will be called a breath, for from breath and falsehood they gathered it; therefore it will be driven away, and they are seekers of death — those who testify falsely. And likewise plunder that others plunder and place the plunder in their treasuries will draw them down to the pit of destruction, as it were; that is, it will break them."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The bracketed [ו-ח] likely marks the letters connecting or separating the three terms; preserved as in source."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:57.897664975Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}